__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,_e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(_e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),_e.PrivacyPolicyBody=function(){const t=(0,e.c)(4);let o,u,y,p;t[0]===Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")?(o=(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{variant:"title",style:{marginTop:8},children:"Privacy Policy"}),t[0]=o):o=t[0];t[1]===Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")?(u=(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{variant:"caption",color:"textMuted",style:{marginTop:4,marginBottom:20},children:"Last updated: [publication date \u2014 to be added]"}),t[1]=u):u=t[1];t[2]===Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")?(y={marginBottom:16},t[2]=y):y=t[2];t[3]===Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")?(p=(0,l.jsxs)(n.default,{testID:"fm-privacy-policy-body",children:[o,u,(0,l.jsxs)(s.Card,{glow:!0,style:y,children:[(0,l.jsx)(s.Eyebrow,{icon:"sparkles",label:"In short",style:{marginBottom:8}}),(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{variant:"body",color:"textMuted",children:"This describes what Cluster collects, why, who within your family can see it, and what happens to it if you delete your account. It is written to match exactly what the app actually stores."})]}),c.map(h)]}),t[3]=p):p=t[3];return p};var e=r(d[0]);r(d[1]);var t,o=r(d[2]),n=(t=o)&&t.__esModule?t:{default:t},s=r(d[3]),l=r(d[4]);const c=[{heading:'Who we are',paragraphs:['Cluster is operated by [the app owner\u2019s legal entity name and address \u2014 to be added]. Questions about this policy or your data: [contact email \u2014 to be added].']},{heading:'What we collect, and why',paragraphs:['Cluster is a shared household app: everything you and your family put into it is stored so that the rest of your family can see it too. That sharing is the product, not a side effect.','Account & sign-in: your email address, and either a securely hashed password or the fact that you signed in with Google, Microsoft, Apple or Facebook. We never see or store your password for any of those accounts.','Your profile: a display name, an optional avatar image, and the timezone and language your device reported. Your display name and avatar are visible to anyone who shares a family with you. Your timezone is used to make reminders and quiet hours land at the correct local time.','Family content: lists, list items, calendar events and reminders, with whatever text you typed into them. This is visible to every member of the family it belongs to, unless it\u2019s on a calendar you marked private, in which case it\u2019s visible only to you.','Availability: you can belong to several groups in Cluster (a family, a class, a team), and nothing you put in one is shown in another. The one exception is when you\u2019re busy. When someone who shares a group with you is choosing a time for an event, Cluster shows them the start and end times of events you\u2019re going to or haven\u2019t declined, in any of your groups and on private calendars too. Only the times are shown \u2014 never an event\u2019s title, place, notes, or which group it belongs to.','Chat: messages you send in your family\u2019s group chat, a smaller group channel, or a direct 1:1 message. A group or family-channel message is visible to that group\u2019s members; a direct message is visible only to the two of you \u2014 never the rest of the family. A thread about one event, list, list item or reminder is visible to everyone in that group who can see the item (for an event on a private calendar, only you), and is deleted with the item. Photos you attach to a chat message are visible to that same audience.','External calendars: if you subscribe a calendar to an external .ics feed, we store the URL you gave us and fetch it on a schedule so events stay current.','Google Calendar: if you connect a Google account to sync calendars (you may connect more than one), we ask Google for permission to see your list of calendars, to see and edit events on your calendars, to create a calendar for Cluster, and to know that Google account\u2019s email address. For each account we store its email address and the access token Google issues, and only ever read or change events on the calendars you choose to add. Their events are visible to you alone, or to your family if you share that calendar, and changes you make to them in Cluster are written back to Google. Our use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements: we use it only to show and sync your calendars, never for advertising, and we don\u2019t sell it. Disconnecting an account in Settings \u2192 Calendars deletes its token and removes its calendars from Cluster; nothing is deleted in Google.','Picture cards: the pictures your family chose for events, and any picture rules, are stored and visible to your family (a choice on a private calendar\u2019s event is visible only to you). A photo you add as a picture card, and its name, are visible to every member of your family. Card pictures are chosen on your device from the event\u2019s title, and \u201cRead aloud\u201d uses your device\u2019s own text-to-speech.','Push notifications: a device token identifying your phone or browser, and a queue of pending notifications addressed to you. The token is sent to Expo\u2019s push notification service, which relays it on to Apple\u2019s or Google\u2019s own delivery infrastructure for your device \u2014 we do not talk to Apple or Google directly for this. Nobody in your family can see your device tokens or notification preferences \u2014 they are yours alone.']},{heading:'Who can see what',paragraphs:['Cluster\u2019s entire access model is enforced by the database itself, not by application code that could have a bug in it. Your account credentials, notification settings and device tokens are yours alone. Your profile is visible to anyone who shares a family with you. Everything else you create is visible only to the members of the specific family, calendar, channel or conversation it belongs to. We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for advertising.']},{heading:'Who else sees it',paragraphs:['We use a small number of service providers to run the app: Supabase hosts our database, authentication, file storage and background jobs. Google, Microsoft, Apple and Facebook are used only if you choose to sign in with them, and Google also receives the calendar changes you make in Cluster if you connect Google Calendar. Expo delivers push notifications on our behalf, relaying them on to Apple\u2019s or Google\u2019s own infrastructure. We do not otherwise share your data with third parties, and we do not use third-party analytics or advertising trackers today.']},{heading:'How long we keep your data',paragraphs:['Family content is kept for as long as your family\u2019s account exists, so the household\u2019s shared history stays intact. You or another member with permission can delete individual items, events or messages you no longer want kept.']},{heading:'Deleting your account',paragraphs:['You can delete your account from Settings \u2192 Account. This is permanent and cannot be undone \u2014 and it is not "everything about you disappears".','What is erased: your login credentials, your profile photo and display name, your device push tokens, your notification preferences, and your membership in every family, chat channel and event you were part of.','What is kept, because it belongs to your family, not just to you: lists, list items, calendar events, calendars, chat channels, chat messages (including group and direct messages), photos you sent in chat, photos you added as picture cards, and reminders you created or were part of. This content is kept and re-attributed to a generic "Deleted member" placeholder in place of your name, so your family keeps working after you leave it.','If you are the only owner of a family that still has other members, you\u2019ll be asked to transfer ownership before you can delete your account. If you are the only member of a family, deleting your account deletes that family too.']},{heading:'Children\u2019s accounts',paragraphs:['Cluster lets a family assign a "teen" or "child" role to a family member. [The app owner should confirm and state here what age range, if any, is permitted to hold their own account, and what parental-consent process applies \u2014 this has not yet been decided in the product.]']},{heading:'Security',paragraphs:['Data in transit between the app and our servers is encrypted (HTTPS/TLS). Access to your data is enforced at the database level for every request. No system is perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.']},{heading:'Your rights',paragraphs:['Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, export or delete your personal data. You can delete your own account and its personal data directly from the app at any time. For any other request, contact us at [contact email \u2014 to be added].']},{heading:'Changes to this policy',paragraphs:['If we make a material change to this policy, we will update its publication date and, where required, notify you in the app.']},{heading:'Contact',paragraphs:['[Company name, mailing address and contact email \u2014 to be added.]']}];function h(e){return(0,l.jsxs)(s.Card,{style:{marginBottom:16},children:[(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{variant:"subtitle",style:{marginBottom:8},children:e.heading}),e.paragraphs.map(u)]},e.heading)}function u(e,t){return(0,l.jsx)(s.Text,{variant:"body",color:"textMuted",style:{marginTop:0===t?0:10},children:e},t)}},2229,[11,13,86,1064,6]);
